      <h3>What a Good Facility Round Record Looks Like</h3>
      <p>Each facility round should be documented with: the date and time, areas covered, team conducting the round, specific observations made (compliant and non-compliant), immediate actions taken, items escalated for follow-up, and the name of the person responsible for closure. NABH assessors will ask to see facility round records — a well-maintained log demonstrates active leadership engagement.</p>
      <p>Rounds conducted but not documented are rounds that did not happen, in NABH's view. The written record is the evidence. Use a structured round form so nothing is missed and every area is consistently assessed.</p>

